<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Burmi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1903</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burmi">Burmi</a> was fought in 1903 in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a> between British colonial forces and followers of the deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> Attahiru I, who had fled after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto</a>. Attahiru was killed in the battle. It marked the final defeat of resistance and the end of the Sokoto Caliphate as an independent state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-burmi.jpg" alt="Battle of Burmi" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:After_the_battle_of_Burmi_(1903).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
